      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "What is __init__ in Python?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In Python, __init__() is a special method that works as a constructor for classes. This method is called automatically when we create an object of a class."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Usually, all the declarations and initializations are done in this method. We do not need to call this method explicitly."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's take a look at an example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1class Person:\n2    def __init__(self):\n3        print('inside __init__ method')\n4\n5obj = Person()\n6\n7# Output:\n8# inside __init__ method"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As you can see, we didn't manually call the __init__() method. The method is called automatically when we create an object of that class."
    },
